  "body": "## What changed\n\nMove the pure machine limit checks to `camcraft-post::machine`.\nMove `MachineCheck`, `REPORT_CAP`, and the shared judgment helpers with them.\nAdd optional operation names and NC line numbers through `SourceLocation`.\nKeep the ECS walk and document-specific checks in app.\nKeep the app diagnostic text and report order.\nAdd no crate dependency.\nRecord the decision in `docs/decisions/2585-machine-judgment.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe limit checks required the app ECS world.\nA stand-alone simulator could not use them with a list of moves and tool values.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe new pins failed before the fix because the pure API did not exist.\nAll five pins pass after the fix:\n\n- `pure_machine_checks_keep_operation_messages_and_nc_line_locations`\n- `pure_tool_checks_keep_rpm_sizes_and_distinct_tool_count`\n- `pure_checks_keep_unstated_limits_inclusive_edges_and_probe_rpm`\n- `pure_travel_uses_origin_flip_and_keeps_posted_lathe_override`\n- `pure_machine_report_caps_findings_and_counts_the_rest`\n\nRestoring the old module made the pins fail. Restoring the fix made them pass.\nEach guard mutation failed an assertion: spindle maximum, spindle minimum, tool length, tool diameter, feed, travel, and tool count.\nAll pins passed after the original guards were restored.\n\nThe final `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all 94 steps.\nThe existing app machine-check assertions did not change.\nThe `machine`, `lathe_stroke`, `fourth_axis_pose`, and `rigid_tapping` suites passed.\nThe mapped UI suites also passed.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe completed checks bypassed a stalled sccache wrapper.\nThe self-review covered all 14 diff hunks.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The `.nc` and `.cl` diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe stand-alone simulator executable and its NC reader are outside this issue.\nThe NC location pin calls the pure API directly.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2554 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt adds separate exports in `crates/post/src/machine/mod.rs`.\nIt does not change the judgment functions.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Machine limit checks can run without an ECS document and locate findings by operation name or NC line number.\n\nFixes #2585\n",
